Input: {"question": "Which educational institution did Teresa Rushe attend?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 55, "text": "As the sun set over the bustling streets of Tehran, Dr."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 56, "end": 183, "text": "Teresa Rushe navigated the crowded campus of Sharif University of Technology, her worn leather satchel slung over her shoulder."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 184, "end": 296, "text": "The scent of cardamom and rosewater wafted from the nearby café, enticing her to pause and collect her thoughts."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 297, "end": 421, "text": "It was a familiar ritual, one she had repeated countless times during her years as a researcher at the esteemed institution."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 422, "end": 611, "text": "Teresa's eyes, a deep shade of indigo, sparkled with a hint of mischief as she recalled the countless late-night debates with her colleagues in the university's cramped, smoke-filled rooms."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 612, "end": 771, "text": "The memories of those fervent discussions, fueled by strong tea and a passion for discovery, still lingered in the air like the faint scent of cigarette smoke."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 772, "end": 936, "text": "As she walked, the sound of her heels clicking on the pavement harmonized with the murmur of students huddled around laptops, their faces aglow in the fading light."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 937, "end": 1156, "text": "The university's iconic windcatchers, towering above the rooftops, seemed to whisper secrets to the wind, their intricate latticework a testament to the ingenuity of the ancient Persian architects who had inspired them."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1157, "end": 1216, "text": "Teresa's thoughts were interrupted by the warm smile of Dr."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1217, "end": 1325, "text": "Amir Hosseini, a fellow researcher and old friend, who emerged from the shadows of the engineering building."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1326, "end": 1434, "text": "\"Teresa, my dear, I see you're still haunting these halls,\" he said, his voice laced with a hint of teasing."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1435, "end": 1474, "text": "\"What brings you back to Sharif today?\""}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1475, "end": 1566, "text": "Teresa's eyes crinkled at the corners as she replied, \"Just dropping off some papers, Amir."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1567, "end": 1603, "text": "I've been meaning to get them to Dr."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1604, "end": 1626, "text": "Karimi for weeks now.\""}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1627, "end": 1787, "text": "The mention of her colleague's name sparked a memory, and she rummaged through her satchel, producing a dog-eared folder emblazoned with the university's crest."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1788, "end": 1877, "text": "\"Speaking of which, have you seen the latest issue of the Journal of Iranian Engineering?"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1878, "end": 1968, "text": "I have an article in it – 'Applications of Nanotechnology in Water Purification Systems'.\""}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1969, "end": 2175, "text": "Amir's eyes lit up with interest, and the two researchers launched into a lively discussion, their conversation weaving in and out of the crowded corridors, leaving a trail of nods and smiles in their wake."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 105, "text": "**Breaking News: Renowned Researcher Teresa Rushe's Academic Roots Traced Back to Prestigious Institute**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 107, "end": 393, "text": "A thorough investigation has confirmed that esteemed researcher Teresa Rushe, known for her groundbreaking work in the field of psychology, has a strong academic foundation rooted in the prestigious Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London, England."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 394, "end": 598, "text": "According to credible sources, including Rushe's own ORCID profile (0000-0002-6640-0977), she has a documented affiliation with the Institute, which is a renowned research school at King's College London."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 599, "end": 793, "text": "This affiliation is further substantiated by Rushe's publication record, which showcases her contributions to various research projects and studies conducted in collaboration with the Institute."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 794, "end": 797, "text": "Dr."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 798, "end": 1041, "text": "Sophia Patel, a colleague of Rushe's and a leading expert in the field of psychology, attested to Rushe's academic background, stating, \"Teresa's work has always been characterized by a deep understanding of the complexities of the human mind."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1042, "end": 1175, "text": "Her time at the Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience undoubtedly played a significant role in shaping her expertise.\""}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1176, "end": 1342, "text": "Data from Rushe's publication record reveals a consistent pattern of collaboration with researchers affiliated with the Institute, further solidifying the connection."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1343, "end": 1528, "text": "A review of her published works shows that she has co-authored multiple papers with Institute researchers, tackling topics such as cognitive psychology and neurodevelopmental disorders."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1529, "end": 1609, "text": "When asked about the significance of Rushe's affiliation with the Institute, Dr."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1610, "end": 1868, "text": "John Taylor, Director of the Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience, commented, \"We take great pride in the accomplishments of our alumni, and Teresa Rushe is an exemplary example of the caliber of researchers who have passed through our doors."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1869, "end": 2008, "text": "Her contributions to the field of psychology are a testament to the Institute's commitment to fostering innovative and impactful research.\""}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2009, "end": 2277, "text": "In conclusion, our investigation has provided conclusive evidence that Teresa Rushe, a respected figure in the research community, has a strong academic foundation rooted in the prestigious Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2278, "end": 2421, "text": "This affiliation has undoubtedly played a significant role in shaping her expertise and contributing to her success in the field of psychology."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Teresa Rushe", "scope": "Educational institution attended", "claim": "Teresa Rushe has a strong academic foundation rooted in the Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London.", "answer": "Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London", "quote": "A thorough investigation has confirmed that esteemed researcher Teresa Rushe, known for her groundbreaking work in the field of psychology, has a strong academic foundation rooted in the prestigious Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London, England. According to credible sources, including Rushe's own ORCID profile (0000-0002-6640-0977), she has a documented affiliation with the Institute, which is a renowned research school at King's College London. This affiliation is further substantiated by Rushe's publication record, which showcases her contributions to various research projects and studies conducted in collaboration with the Institute. Dr. Sophia Patel, a colleague of Rushe's and a leading expert in the field of psychology, attested to Rushe's academic background, stating, \"Teresa's work has always been characterized by a deep understanding of the complexities of the human mind. Her time at the Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience undoubtedly played a significant role in shaping her expertise.\" Data from Rushe's publication record reveals a consistent pattern of collaboration with researchers affiliated with the Institute, further solidifying the connection. A review of her published works shows that she has co-authored multiple papers with Institute researchers, tackling topics such as cognitive psychology and neurodevelopmental disorders. When asked about the significance of Rushe's affiliation with the Institute, Dr. John Taylor, Director of the Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience, commented, \"We take great pride in the accomplishments of our alumni, and Teresa Rushe is an exemplary example of the caliber of researchers who have passed through our doors.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Institute of Psychiatry, Psychology and Neuroscience at King's College London", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
